# Example 1-14 from 'Computer Mapping as an Aid in Air Pollution Studies',
# Vol. 2, Report K (Harvard Laboratory for Computer Graphics, 1971), pp. 29-30.
# Two proximal maps; the second deletes the legends and uses elective 7
# to strike black precinct boundaries on a dashed background.
# The scale-bar text cards are given as the map (Example 1-16) prints them:
# 'I' at the ends and '+' at the midpoint. The listing printer shows ')'
# and a bold dot for these, and the same dot for the canal's '+=' (the
# Example 1-20 listing, printed more clearly, shows '+='), so the two
# printers' character sets differ.
